ShapeFix_IntersectionTool::FixSelfIntersectWire: the edges of the wire
are read into an array once instead of by number from the wire's
sequence for every pair of edges (mitcad#642).

The search for intersections of non-adjacent edges of a wire reads, for
every pair of edge numbers num1 < num2, edge num1 and edge num2 from
ShapeExtend_WireData. The wire keeps its edges in an NCollection_Sequence,
whose access by number walks node by node from the place read last (or
from the nearer end), so each pair walked about twice the distance between
num1 and num2: the work grew with the cube of the number of edges, and on
the long wires of a body with hundreds of ribs it was the larger part of
healing the body.

The edges are now read into an array in one walk and taken from it by
number. The fixes of the loop change the wire (split edges, union their
vertices, remove segments) only for a pair whose edges intersect at a
point or along a segment; the array is read again after such a pair, so
every later pair sees the wire as the fixes left it, as before.
